<h2>Prestige and Career Path</h2>
<p><a href="https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ergo/12405314.0005.010?view=text;rgn=main&amp;ref=apda.ghost.io" rel="noreferrer">A 2018 paper by Helen De Cruz</a> and <a href="https://jonathanweisberg.org/post/prestige-placement/?ref=apda.ghost.io" rel="noreferrer">a 2019 analysis by Jonathan Weisberg</a> both explored the role prestige (as approximated by the Philosophical Gourmet Report ranking) plays in the academic job market. Following De Cruz, I put institutions into three categories based on the 2021 <a href="https://philosophicalgourmet.com/overall-rankings/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Philosophical Gourmet Report</a> (PGR) (accessed 2026-03-20: table &#8220;in the English speaking world&#8221;): PGR 1-20, PGR 21-50, and PGR unranked.<a href="#fn1">[1]</a> <a href="#fn2">[2]</a></p>
